## Data Preparation

Each row represents one unique content page aggregated across the selected month.

The available features describe the search performance of each page, including impressions, clicks, average ranking position, and CTR. These observed search signals form the basis for the machine learning model.

Before training, additional business-oriented features are engineered to better represent search opportunity.

position_bins = [0,3,10,20,float("inf")]

position_labels = [
    "1-3",
    "4-10",
    "11-20",
    "21+"
]

model_df["position_bucket"] = pd.cut(

    model_df["avg_position"],
    bins=position_bins,
    labels=position_labels,
    include_lowest=True

)
bucket_ctr = (

    model_df
    .groupby("position_bucket", observed=False)["ctr"]
    .median()
    .reset_index(name="bucket_median_ctr")

)

bucket_ctr

model_df = model_df.merge(

    bucket_ctr,

    on="position_bucket",

    how="left"

)

model_df["log_impressions"] = np.log1p(
    model_df["total_impressions"]
)

model_df["position_inverse"] = (
    1/model_df["avg_position"]
)

model_df["ctr_gap"] = (
    model_df["bucket_median_ctr"]
    -
    model_df["ctr"]
)

THRESHOLD = model_df["total_impressions"].quantile(0.75)

model_df["opportunity_label"] = (

    (model_df["total_impressions"]>=THRESHOLD)

    &

    (model_df["total_clicks"]==0)

).astype(int)

print(model_df["opportunity_label"].value_counts())

